<template id="study-limitations-content">
  <div class="report-prose">
    <h3>Limited evaluation budget</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Usage quotas limited the breadth of testing.</strong> The main evaluation covers all
      26 tasks and 510 episodes, but broader repeated runs, additional configurations and controlled
      ablations remain limited.
    </p>
    <h3>Coupled benchmark dimensions</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Some evaluation dimensions in EBench are coupled</strong>, so numerical results alone
      cannot fully explain differences in the models’ capabilities. We complement the results with{' '}
      <strong>case analyses of execution videos</strong> to explain these capability differences and
      support our conclusions. The differences also motivate further investigation into the
      capabilities and behaviors behind them.
    </p>
    <h3>Cross-episode experience</h3>
    <p>
      Each episode starts with a fresh history. The study{' '}
      <strong>does not compare cross-episode skill accumulation</strong>, persistent memory or
      experience-derived tools. Within-episode correction and self-summary are observable here;
      transfer to later tasks remains a separate question.
    </p>
    <h3>Embodied harness integration</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Results combining GPT-6-Astra with embodied harness frameworks are not yet reported here.
      </strong>{' '}
      This page compares the evaluated control interface with baseline policies. The agent–policy
      combinations discussed in the conclusion are research directions motivated by these findings.
    </p>
  </div>
</template>
